# Per-user topic permissions.
#
# The mesh protocol lives under a leading slash (/relay, /switch, /blind,
# /heating). The Home Assistant bridge publishes only under homeassistant/ and
# domator/, with no leading slash, so the two never overlap -- which is what
# lets Home Assistant share this broker without being able to reach the mesh.

# The backend is the only thing that bridges between the two worlds.
user turbacz
topic readwrite #

# ESP-WiFi-mesh root node (uc/buttonsMeshIDF).
user mesh_root
topic readwrite /relay/#
topic readwrite /switch/#

# Heating controller (uc/heating).
user heating-wifi
topic write /heating/metrics
topic read /heating/cmd

# Legacy blind controller (uc/blinds_wifi).
user blinds-wifi
topic write /blind/pos
topic read /blind/cmd

# Home Assistant: discovery and the bridge's own topic tree, nothing else.
# It cannot see or command the mesh directly.
user homeassistant
topic readwrite homeassistant/#
topic readwrite domator/#
